{"images":["data:image/webp;base64,"],"messages":[{"content":"A 31-year-old G2 P1 woman gives birth at 38 weeks gestational age to a male infant. However, the placenta cannot be delivered, and there is extensive hemorrhage. She undergoes emergent hysterectomy, and the gross appearance of the uterus is shown here. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis? <image> \n\n(A) Abruptio placenta\n(B) Placenta accreta\n(C) Chorioamnionitis\n(D) Twin placenta\n(E) Partial mole\n\nAnswer with the option's letter from the given choices directly.","role":"user"}]}